    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded by the Kurdish commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>, it united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-mesopotamia">Upper Mesopotamia</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader states</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin">Hattin</a> and recapture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 1187 permanently shifted the balance in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>.</li><li>Divided among quarrelling kinsmen, it was overthrown by its own mamluk soldiers in 1250 and finished by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s nephew, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil">al-Kamil</a>, later handed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> to Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> by treaty in 1229, in return for help against his own Ayyubid relatives.</p></aside>
    </section>

