 takes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1192</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jaffa-1192">Treaty of Jaffa</a> ends the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> still in Ayyubid hands</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1193</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> dies, triggering a succession struggle among his sons</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1229</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil">Al-Kamil</a> cedes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Holy Roman Emperor Frederick II</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1250</span><span class="rf-text">Bahri mamluks murder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turanshah">Turanshah</a> and seize <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1259–1260</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> invade the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>, sack <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> and end Ayyubid rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a></span></li></ol>
